Looking at the myth I just wrote about the Guardian of Giving taking "a leap of faith," I should practice what I preached in my story. Trust must begin somewhere, and the first guardian had to move first.

Sending a meaningful amount demonstrates trust and gives the receiver substantial resources ($9 after tripling) to work with. If they return fairly, we both benefit more than if I had been cautious.

